<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Memnon of Heraclea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st or 2nd century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Memnon of Heraclea was a Greek historian, probably of the 1st or 2nd century CE, who wrote a history of his city, Heraclea Pontica. Its books 9 to 16 survive in a summary by the Byzantine patriarch Photius, covering events from the tyranny of Clearchus to the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. It is an important source for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> region and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mithridatic-wars">Mithridatic Wars</a>.</p></div>
